% ============================================================================
% phase-change-alt-name.query.adj — a worked recall over the physics
% phase-change-alt-name library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what's an older word
% for melting?": it states no physics fact of its own — it only `import`s
% the grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?`
% against the `phase_change_alt_name` rows and returns the alternate name +
% the table's source/locator/trust. A direction the cited spans give no
% alternate name for abstains honestly — the engine never invents a
% synonym.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli phase-change-alt-name.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "phase-change-alt-name.adj"

? phase_change_alt_name(solid_to_liquid, $AltName)   % expect fusion
? phase_change_alt_name($Change, boiling)            % reverse bind — expect liquid_to_gas
? phase_change_alt_name(gas_to_liquid, $AltName)     % expect abstain — the cited span names condensation only, no alternate word
